{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgcXbFnAfB4JjPejoyWJe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RgS5RZKAzDocnoF8mPYDNP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/traccar/repo && mkdir -p docs/decisions docs/harness && cat > docs/decisions/0001-record-architecture-decisions.md <<'EOF'\n# 1. Record architecture decisions\n\nDate: 2026-11-01\n\nStatus: accepted\n\n## Context\n\nTraccar has more than 10,000 commits and very few written explanations of why the code is shaped the way it is. New contributors and coding agents must guess, and they guess wrong on things like schema changes or where to put a new protocol.\n\n## Decision\n\nWe keep short architecture decision records in `docs/decisions/`, one Markdown file per decision, numbered `NNNN-short-title.md`. Each record has:\n\n- **Context**: the problem and the forces at play.\n- **Decision**: what we do, in one or two paragraphs.\n- **Consequences**: what gets easier, what gets harder, what to watch.\n\nA record is never rewritten after it is accepted. When a decision changes, a new record supersedes the old one and the old one gets `Status: superseded by NNNN`.\n\nRecords that describe a decision found in the code but never written down by the team say \"Inferred from the code, to be confirmed by the team.\"\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Agents and humans can read why before they change how.\n- A pull request that changes an important design choice should add a record.\nEOF\ncat > docs/decisions/0002-one-netty-decoder-per-protocol.md <<'EOF'\n# 2. One Netty pipeline, decoder and test per device protocol\n\nDate: 2026-11-01\n\nStatus: inferred from the code, to be confirmed by the team.\n\n## Context\n\nTraccar supports more than 200 device protocols. Devices speak binary or text formats over TCP, UDP, HTTP or MQTT, and many vendors change their formats over time. Each protocol needs its own framing and parsing, and a bug in one must not break the others.\n\n## Decision\n\nEach protocol is a set of classes in `src/main/java/org/traccar/protocol/`:\n\n- `<Name>Protocol` extends `BaseProtocol`, declares supported commands and adds one or more `TrackerServer` listeners with their Netty handlers.\n- `<Name>FrameDecoder` (when needed) splits the stream into messages.\n- `<Name>ProtocolDecoder` extends `BaseProtocolDecoder` (or the HTTP/MQTT variants) and returns `Position` objects.\n- `<Name>ProtocolEncoder` (when the device accepts commands).\n- The protocol is registered with its default port in `src/main/java/org/traccar/config/ProtocolConfig.java`.\n- `src/test/java/org/traccar/protocol/<Name>ProtocolDecoderTest` extends `ProtocolTest` and replays real messages as hex or text.\n\nEvery protocol runs on its own port, so a device never needs to be identified before decoding.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- A new protocol or a format change is local to a few files and one test class.\n- The `protocol` package is very large (about 680 files). Shared parsing helpers live in `src/main/java/org/traccar/helper/` (`Parser`, `PatternBuilder`, `BitUtil`, `Checksum`, `UnitsConverter`); reuse them instead of writing new ones.\n- A server opens hundreds of ports by default. `protocols.enable` limits them.\n- Decoder tests are fast and offline, which makes `./gradlew test` a usable fast gate.\nEOF\ncat > docs/decisions/0003-liquibase-schema-for-several-databases.md <<'EOF'\n# 3. Liquibase changelogs for a schema shared by several databases\n\nDate: 2026-11-01\n\nStatus: inferred from the code, to be confirmed by the team.\n\n## Context\n\nSelf-hosted users run Traccar on the database they already have. `build.gradle` ships JDBC drivers for H2, MySQL, MariaDB, PostgreSQL and SQL Server. The server must create and upgrade its schema by itself during an upgrade, without a manual migration step.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe schema is defined by Liquibase XML changelogs in `schema/`. `schema/changelog-master.xml` includes one `changelog-<version>.xml` per release that changed the schema. `src/main/java/org/traccar/storage/DatabaseModule.java` runs Liquibase at startup. Queries are built by `storage/QueryBuilder` and `storage/DatabaseStorage` from the model classes (`@StorageName` gives the table), not hand-written per database.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Upgrading is \"install the new version and start it\".\n- Released changelogs must never be edited: Liquibase stores checksums. Changes go into a new changeset.\n- A changeset must work on every supported database. The unit tests do not run against MySQL, PostgreSQL or SQL Server, so cross-database breakage is not caught by CI. `compose.yaml` gives local PostgreSQL and MySQL to test by hand.\n- Rolling back a release that changed the schema is not automatic.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write decision records"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1107,"cache_read_input_tokens":99875,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1107},"output_tokens":40,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38d1d7b6-d88d-475c-865f-50e7106ad4d2","uuid":"265d330a-71e7-404f-a1aa-ace9a5a1a509","timestamp":"2026-11-01T16:32:25.024Z","request_id":"req_011CgcXbFX3LmqvY385aib8W","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RgS5RZKAzDocnoF8mPYDNP":{"command":"cd /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/traccar/repo && mkdir -p docs/decisions docs/harness && cat > docs/decisions/0001-record-architecture-decisions.md <<'EOF'\n# 1. Record architecture decisions\n\nDate: 2026-11-01\n\nStatus: accepted\n\n## Context\n\nTraccar has more than 10,000 commits and very few written explanations of why the code is shaped the way it is. New contributors and coding a