{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012Brwf1yc51AtcqxZzXVYu6","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/traccar/repo/docs/observability.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38d1d7b6-d88d-475c-865f-50e7106ad4d2","uuid":"3f52ff2c-4f9d-4364-9733-ae3e7612d377","timestamp":"2026-11-01T16:33:29.949Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/traccar/repo/docs/observability.md","oldString":"the server calls `/api/health` and notifies the systemd watchdog only on HTTP 200. After one hour of failed checks systemd restarts the service. `web.disableHealthCheck` turns it off.","newString":"the server calls `/api/health` and notifies the systemd watchdog only on HTTP 200 (always during the first hour after start). When systemd gets no notification for 600 seconds, it restarts the service. `web.disableHealthCheck` turns it off.","originalFile":"# Observability\n\nWhat the code shows about logs, health and metrics. Where production logs, dashboards and alerts live is not visible in this repository.\n\n## Logs\n\n- Library: SLF4J over `java.util.logging` (`org.slf4j:slf4j-jdk14`), set up by `src/main/java/org/traccar/helper/Log.java`.\n- Configuration keys (`src/main/java/org/traccar/config/Keys.java`):\n  - `logger.console`: log to stdout (on in `debug.xml`).\n  - `logger.file`: log file, default `./logs/tracker-server.log`. Installers write to `/opt/traccar/logs` (mounted as a volume in `docker/compose/*.yaml`).\n  - `logger.level`: default `info`.\n  - `logger.rotate`, `logger.rotate.interval` (`day` by default): one log file per period.\n  - `logger.fullStackTraces`: full stack traces instead of one line.\n  - `logger.queries`: log SQL queries.\n  - `logger.decodeTextData`, `logger.attributes`: what is logged for each decoded message (`helper/PositionLogger.java`).\n- Format: one line per record, `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS LEVEL: message`. Each device message is logged with its connection id, protocol and hex or text payload.\n- HTTP request log: `web.requestLog.path` and `web.requestLog.retainDays`.\n- Under systemd the journal also holds stdout (`SyslogIdentifier=traccar` in `setup/traccar.service`).\n\n## Health\n\n- `GET /api/health` (`api/resource/HealthResource.java`, no login): returns `OK` with HTTP 200, or HTTP 500 when the database query on `tc_servers` fails, or when `web.healthCheck.dropThreshold` is set and the number of stored messages in the last period fell below that ratio of the previous period.\n- `schedule/TaskHealthCheck.java`: under systemd (`WatchdogSec=600` in `setup/traccar.service`), the server calls `/api/health` and notifies the systemd watchdog only on HTTP 200. After one hour of failed checks systemd restarts the service. `web.disableHealthCheck` turns it off.\n- The example compose stacks use the same endpoint as a Docker healthcheck, with `autoheal` restarting unhealthy containers.\n\n## Metrics\n\n- `StatisticsManager` (`database/StatisticsManager.java`) counts requests, messages received and stored, active users and devices, and writes a daily row to `tc_statistics`.\n- `GET /api/statistics?from=...&to=...` (`api/resource/StatisticsResource.java`, administrators) returns those rows.\n- There is no Prometheus or OpenTelemetry exporter on `master`. A remote branch `codex/add-prometheus-metrics-endpoint` exists but is not merged.\n\n## Error reporting\n\nNo Sentry or similar client is in `build.gradle`. Errors go to the log only (`Thread exception`, `Main method error`).\n\n## How to tell that something is wrong\n\n1. `curl -fsS http://<host>:8082/api/health` does not return `OK`.\n2. The number of stored messages drops (the `dropThreshold` check above, or `messagesStored` in `/api/statistics`).\n3. `ERROR` or `WARN` lines in the log, for example `Port ... disabled due to conflict` at startup, or database errors.\n4. Devices go offline in bulk (device status in the web UI, `deviceOffline` events).\n\n## Production\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Needs a human.** For the managed service, where are logs, metrics and alerts kept, and which signal tells you production is broken (only /api/health, or something else)?\n> Why it matters and how to do it: https://docs.unwritten.sh/harness/guides/observability/\n<!-- uw-harness:todo observability -->\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":20,"oldLines":7,"newStart":20,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ## Health"," "," - `GET /api/health` (`api/resource/HealthResource.java`, no login): returns `OK` with HTTP 200, or HTTP 500 when the database query on `tc_servers` fails, or when `web.healthCheck.dropThreshold` is set and the number of stored messages in the last period fell below that ratio of the previous period.","-- `schedule/TaskHealthCheck.java`: under systemd (`WatchdogSec=600` in `setup/traccar.service`), the server calls `/api/health` and notifies the systemd watchdog only on HTTP 200. After one hour of failed checks systemd restarts the service. `web.disableHealthCheck` turns it off.","+- `schedule/TaskHealthCheck.java`: under systemd (`WatchdogSec=600` in `setup/traccar.service`), the server calls `/api/health` and notifies the systemd watchdog only on HTTP 200 (always during the first hour after start). When systemd gets no notification for 600 seconds, it restarts the service. `web.disableHealthCheck` turns it off."," - The example compose stacks use the same endpoint as a Docker healthcheck, with `autoheal` restarting unhealthy containers."," "," ## Metrics"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012Brwf1yc51AtcqxZzXVYu6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
