r database errors.\n4. Devices go offline in bulk (device status in the web UI, `deviceOffline` events).\n\n## Production\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Needs a human.** For the managed service, where are logs, metrics and alerts kept, and which signal tells you production is broken (only /api/health, or something else)?\n> Why it matters and how to do it: https://docs.unwritten.sh/harness/guides/observability/\n<!-- uw-harness:todo observability -->\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":25,"oldLines":7,"newStart":25,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## Metrics"," ","-- `StatisticsManager` (`database/StatisticsManager.java`) counts requests, messages received and stored, active users and devices, and writes a daily row to `tc_statistics`.","+- `StatisticsManager` (`database/StatisticsManager.java`) counts requests, messages received and stored, active users and devices, mail, SMS, geocoder and geolocation requests, and writes a daily row to `tc_statistics`. When `server.statistics` is set, it also posts the same anonymous numbers to that URL."," - `GET /api/statistics?from=...&to=...` (`api/resource/StatisticsResource.java`, administrators) returns those rows."," - There is no Prometheus or OpenTelemetry exporter on `master`. A remote branch `codex/add-prometheus-metrics-endpoint` exists but is not merged."," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P2B7CrQZKpEXrgsUQJVnBZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
