(\"...\"), Position.KEY_POWER, 12.5);\n   ```","new_string":"   verifyDecode(decoder, binary(\"78780D01086471700328358100093F040D0A\"));   // no position expected\n   verifyDecode(decoder, binary(\"7979...0d0a\"),\n           position(Checks.ATTRIBUTES).attribute(Position.KEY_POWER, 4.05));\n   ```\n   The number of `position(...)` arguments is the number of positions expected. `Checks.ALL` also checks time and coordinates, `Checks.ATTRIBUTES` only the attributes you list, `Checks.NONE` nothing but the count. See `src/test/java/org/traccar/ProtocolTest.java`."}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016oheeJBPJBYontzrt7ehVE","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/traccar/repo/.agents/skills/add-protocol-decoder/SKILL.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38d1d7b6-d88d-475c-865f-50e7106ad4d2","uuid":"dee18756-d643-4217-805a-6d67799b9442","timestamp":"2026-11-01T16:34:40.906Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/traccar/repo/.agents/skills/add-protocol-decoder/SKILL.md","oldString":"   verifyPosition(decoder, binary(\"78780D01086471700328358100093F040D0A\"));\n   verifyAttribute(decoder, text(\"...\"), Position.KEY_POWER, 12.5);\n   ```","newString":"   verifyDecode(decoder, binary(\"78780D01086471700328358100093F040D0A\"));   // no position expected\n   verifyDecode(decoder, binary(\"7979...0d0a\"),\n           position(Checks.ATTRIBUTES).attribute(Position.KEY_POWER, 4.05));\n   ```\n   The number of `position(...)` arguments is the number of positions expected. `Checks.ALL` also checks time and coordinates, `Checks.ATTRIBUTES` only the attributes you list, `Checks.NONE` nothing but the count. See `src/test/java/org/traccar/ProtocolTest.java`.","originalFile":"---\nname: add-protocol-decoder\ndescription: Use when adding a new device protocol or changing how an existing protocol decodes messages or encodes commands.\n---\n\n# Add or change a protocol decoder\n\nBackground: [docs/decisions/0002-one-netty-decoder-per-protocol.md](../../../docs/decisions/0002-one-netty-decoder-per-protocol.md).\n\n1. Get a real sample message from the task or issue (hex for binary, text otherwise). Do not invent sample data: if there is none, stop and ask.\n2. Look for an existing protocol with the same format first: `grep -ril \"<vendor or keyword>\" src/main/java/org/traccar/protocol`. Many devices reuse GT06, H02, Teltonika, Meitrack or similar formats; extending a decoder is better than adding a protocol.\n3. To change an existing protocol, add the sample to `src/test/java/org/traccar/protocol/<Name>ProtocolDecoderTest.java` first, for example:\n   ```java\n   verifyPosition(decoder, binary(\"78780D01086471700328358100093F040D0A\"));\n   verifyAttribute(decoder, text(\"...\"), Position.KEY_POWER, 12.5);\n   ```\n   Run it and see it fail: `make test TESTS=org.traccar.protocol.Gt06ProtocolDecoderTest`.\n4. For a new protocol, create in `src/main/java/org/traccar/protocol/`, copying a similar protocol:\n   - `<Name>Protocol.java` extends `BaseProtocol`; adds a `TrackerServer` (second argument `true` for UDP) and its handlers in `addProtocolHandlers`.\n   - `<Name>FrameDecoder.java` if the transport is a stream with no simple delimiter (otherwise use `CharacterDelimiterFrameDecoder` or `LineBasedFrameDecoder` in the pipeline).\n   - `<Name>ProtocolDecoder.java` extends `BaseProtocolDecoder`; use `getDeviceSession(...)`, `Parser`/`PatternBuilder` for text, `ByteBuf` and `BitUtil` for binary.\n   - `<Name>ProtocolEncoder.java` only if the device accepts commands, and list them with `setSupportedDataCommands`.\n5. Register a new protocol in `src/main/java/org/traccar/config/ProtocolConfig.java`: add the import and `put(<Name>Protocol.class, <port>);` with the next free port after the last entry.\n6. Create `src/test/java/org/traccar/protocol/<Name>ProtocolDecoderTest.java` (extends `ProtocolTest`, `var decoder = inject(new <Name>ProtocolDecoder(null));`) and, if there is a frame decoder, `<Name>FrameDecoderTest.java`.\n7. Use the standard keys in `src/main/java/org/traccar/model/Position.java` (`KEY_*`, `ALARM_*`) before inventing attribute names.\n8. Run `make check-fast`. Checkstyle often flags line length and import order in decoders.\n9. Optional end-to-end check: `make dev`, then send the sample with `tools/hex.sh <port> <hex>` and look for the decoded position in the console log.\n10. Commit as `Decode <vendor> <message type>` or `Add <Name> protocol`, following `CONTRIBUTING.md`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":11,"oldLines":9,"newStart":11,"newLines":11,"lines":[" 2. Look for an existing protocol with the same format first: `grep -ril \"<vendor or keyword>\" src/main/java/org/traccar/protocol`. Many devices reuse GT06, H02, Teltonika, Meitrack or similar formats; extending a decoder is better than adding a protocol."," 3. To change an existing protocol, add the sample to `src/test/java/org/traccar/protocol/<Name>ProtocolDecoderTest.java` first, for example:","    ```java","-   verifyPosition(decoder, binary(\"78780D01086471700328358100093F040D0A\"));","-   verifyAttribute(decoder, text(\"...\"), Position.KEY_POWER, 12.5);","+   verifyDecode(decoder, binary(\"78780D01086471700328358100093F040D0A\"));   // no position expected","+   verifyDecode(decoder, binary(\"7979...0d0a\"),","+           position(Checks.ATTRIBUTES).attribute(Position.KEY_POWER, 4.05));","    ```","+   The number of `position(...)` arguments is the number of positions expected. `Checks.ALL` also checks time and coordinates, `Checks.ATTRIBUTES` only the attributes you list, `Checks.NONE` nothing but the count. See `src/test/java/org/traccar/ProtocolTest.java`.","    Run it and see it fail: `make test TESTS=org.traccar.protocol.Gt06ProtocolDecoderTest`."," 4. For a new protocol, create in `src/main/java/org/traccar/protocol/`, copying a similar protocol:","    - `<Name>Protocol.java` extends `BaseProtocol`; adds a `TrackerServer` (second argument `true` for UDP) and its handlers in `addProtocolHandlers`."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016oheeJBPJBYontzrt7ehVE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
